    "result_text": "All green \u2014 the full suite passes (17 tests, 0 failures) with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `customerCode` assignment on `POST /api/owners`, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **New OfficeFloor function** \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.java`: reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, computes the sequence as `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` (one more than the current owner count, so it excludes the not-yet-saved owner), and sets `customerCode` to `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, sequence)`. `LAST3` is the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (guarded for short names).\n\n2. **Wired it into the pipeline** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted an `assignCustomerCode` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `build` and `save`, so the code is computed before persistence and committed with the new owner.\n\n3. **Persisted the field** \u2014 added `customerCode` (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) plus getter/setter to the `Owner` entity, and a `customer_code` column to all four `schema.sql` files (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\n4. **Exposed it on the response** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field; MapStruct maps it by name, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it.\n\nThe global sequence is consistent with the existing `EnsureUniqueTelephone` rule, which likewise reads `findAll()` across creates within a request/test \u2014 so the new `Cp09Tests.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` (SMI-/JON- prefixes, consecutive sequence numbers) passes without disturbing the other checkpoints.",
